4.2.2 Ethnicity of Ugandans
Ethnicity is the state of belonging to a social group with comm on culture, tradition and
language. Ugandans are classified by ethnic groups as listed in  the Constitution of the
Republic of Uganda. The Baganda are the majority accounting for close to 17 percent of the
population followed by the Banyankole with about 10 percent as shown in table 4.3. Detailed
population by ethnicity is presented in Appendix Table A8.
